  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "A delimited record is copied out of the parser's buffer once, as one string, and each of its values is parsed as a slice of that string rather than copied into a string of its own; a value whose characters are not next to each other in the record, because of a doubled quote or whitespace kept from around it, is rebuilt as before. Around 8% less allocation on a delimited read and eleven fewer objects per record, with unchanged results and unchanged time. PreserveRecordText now costs nothing. No API changes. Source- and binary-compatible with 7.5.0.",
